  "summary": "Muhammad Shaybani Khan, an Uzbek ruler descended from Genghis Khan, had by 1500 made himself master of Samarkand and the Syr Darya and Amu Darya basins. He then advanced into Khorasan and took Herat in 1507, ending Timurid rule there. He was killed by the Safavid shah Ismail I in 1510.",
